/*!
\page page_stFtpcHitCollection StFtpcHitCollection

\ref StFtpcHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed hits in the STAR Forward
Time Projection Chambers (FTPC). Hits are stored in a three-level hierarchy —
<b>plane → sector → hit</b> — reflecting the FTPC readout geometry of radial drift planes each
divided into azimuthal sectors. The two supporting classes, \ref StFtpcPlaneHitCollection and
\ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection, are internal nodes of that hierarchy and are not used
independently.

\section sec_ftpc_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StFtpcHitCollection          (top level, 20 planes)
└── StFtpcPlaneHitCollection     (one per plane, 6 sectors each)
    └── StFtpcSectorHitCollection    (one per sector, holds StFtpcHit* pointers)
\endverbatim

All three classes inherit from StObject.

\section sec_ftpc_containment Containment Model

- \ref StFtpcHitCollection holds an embedded array of 20 \ref StFtpcPlaneHitCollection objects
  (<tt>mPlanes[20]</tt>).
- Each \ref StFtpcPlaneHitCollection holds an embedded array of 6 \ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection
  objects (<tt>mSectors[6]</tt>).
- Each \ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection holds a dynamic <tt>StSPtrVecFtpcHit mHits</tt> vector of
  pointers to \ref StFtpcHit objects.

\ref StFtpcHitCollection::addHit "addHit(StFtpcHit*)" routes an \ref StFtpcHit into the correct
<tt>mHits</tt> vector using the hit's own 1-based <tt>plane()</tt> and <tt>sector()</tt>
accessors, converting internally to 0-based array indices. The public accessor methods
<tt>plane()</tt> and <tt>sector()</tt> use <b>0-based</b> indices.

\section sec_ftpc_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection subsec_ftpc_subcoll Sub-collection Storage
\ref StFtpcPlaneHitCollection and \ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection objects are
<b>stack-allocated as plain arrays</b> inside their parent. They are not heap-allocated and must
not be deleted by the caller.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_hits Hit Storage — StSPtrVecFtpcHit
The per-sector hit vector is of type <tt>StSPtrVecFtpcHit</tt>, a <em>smart-pointer vector</em>.
\ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection::~StFtpcSectorHitCollection "~StFtpcSectorHitCollection()" iterates
over the vector and explicitly <tt>delete</tt>s each <tt>StFtpcHit*</tt>. This explicit deletion
is required because \ref StFtpcHit uses a custom <tt>new</tt>/<tt>delete</tt> via
<tt>StMemoryPool</tt>.

\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StFtpcHit pointers obtained from the collection.
Ownership belongs to \ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection; external deletion will cause a double-free.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_framework Framework Ownership
\ref StFtpcHitCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework (via the
<tt>St_DataSet</tt>/<tt>StXRefMain</tt> mechanism). When registered with StEvent via
<tt>StEvent::setFtpcHitCollection()</tt>, ownership transfers to the framework, which handles
cleanup. <tt>StFtpcHitCollection::~StFtpcHitCollection()</tt> and
<tt>StFtpcPlaneHitCollection::~StFtpcPlaneHitCollection()</tt> are no-ops; only
\ref StFtpcSectorHitCollection performs explicit hit cleanup.

\section sec_ftpc_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_ftpc_members_top StFtpcHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mNumberOfPlanes = 20 }</tt> — Fixed number of FTPC readout planes.
- <tt>StFtpcPlaneHitCollection mPlanes[20]</tt> — Embedded array of per-plane collections.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_members_plane StFtpcPlaneHitCollection
- <tt>enum { mNumberOfSectors = 6 }</tt> — Number of azimuthal sectors per plane.
- <tt>StFtpcSectorHitCollection mSectors[6]</tt> — Embedded array of per-sector collections.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_members_sector StFtpcSectorHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecFtpcHit mHits</tt> — Dynamic vector of pointers to \ref StFtpcHit objects in this
  sector.

\section sec_ftpc_methods Key Methods

\subsection subsec_ftpc_methods_top StFtpcHitCollection
- <tt>bool addHit(StFtpcHit*)</tt> — Routes a hit into the correct plane/sector sub-collection.
  Returns <tt>false</tt> if the hit is null or its indices are out of range.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits across all planes and sectors.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfPlanes() const</tt> — Returns 20.
- <tt>StFtpcPlaneHitCollection* plane(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index, or
  <tt>nullptr</tt> if out of range.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_methods_plane StFtpcPlaneHitCollection
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfHits() const</tt> — Total hits in this plane.
- <tt>unsigned int numberOfSectors() const</tt> — Returns 6.
- <tt>StFtpcSectorHitCollection* sector(unsigned int)</tt> — Sub-collection at 0-based index.

\subsection subsec_ftpc_methods_sector StFtpcSectorHitCollection
- <tt>StSPtrVecFtpcHit& hits()</tt> — Mutable reference to the hit vector.
- <tt>const StSPtrVecFtpcHit& hits() const</tt> — Const reference to the hit vector.

\section sec_ftpc_usage Usage Examples

\subsection subsec_ftpc_usage_iter Iterate Over All Hits

\code{.cpp}
StFtpcHitCollection* ftpcColl = event->ftpcHitCollection();
if (!ftpcColl) return;

for (unsigned int iPlane = 0; iPlane < ftpcColl->numberOfPlanes(); ++iPlane) {
    const StFtpcPlaneHitCollection* plane = ftpcColl->plane(iPlane);
    if (!plane) continue;

    for (unsigned int iSec = 0; iSec < plane->numberOfSectors(); ++iSec) {
        const StFtpcSectorHitCollection* sec = plane->sector(iSec);
        if (!sec) continue;

        const StSPtrVecFtpcHit& hits = sec->hits();
        for (const StFtpcHit* hit : hits) {
            // process hit -- do NOT delete hit
        }
    }
}
\endcode

\subsection subsec_ftpc_usage_add Add a Hit (e.g. from a Maker)

\code{.cpp}
StFtpcHit* hit = new StFtpcHit(/*...*/);  // allocated via StFtpcHit::operator new
ftpcColl->addHit(hit);                    // ownership transferred to the collection
// Do not delete 'hit' after this call.
\endcode

*/
